  "request": {
    "spec": "Unify the customerCode and membershipNumber into a single 'memberId' formatted '<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>': the region code, the 2-digit fiscal year, the 8 upper-hex HASH8 (the same SHA-256-over-(normalizedTelephone+lastName) first-8-hex used by the region-and-hash identity), and a single Luhn check digit CHK computed over the digits of <REGION><FY><HASH8>. Remove the separate customerCode and membershipNumber fields, and also remove the standalone 'checkDigit' field (it was derived from the now-removed customerCode; its Luhn digit is now the CHK segment inside memberId). This changes existing behaviour: collision handling applies to the memberId, and the fiscal-year value, the audit record and the owner segment must all reference the memberId.",
    "prompt": "Implement the following change to the application so that it fully satisfies\nthe specification and all existing and new tests pass. Run the test suite and\nmake it green before finishing.\n\nUnify the customerCode and membershipNumber into a single 'memberId' formatted '<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>': the region code, the 2-digit fiscal year, the 8 upper-hex HASH8 (the same SHA-256-over-(normalizedTelephone+lastName) first-8-hex used by the region-and-hash identity), and a single Luhn check digit CHK computed over the digits of <REGION><FY><HASH8>. Remove the separate customerCode and membershipNumber fields, and also remove the standalone 'checkDigit' field (it was derived from the now-removed customerCode; its Luhn digit is now the CHK segment inside memberId). This changes existing behaviour: collision handling applies to the memberId, and the fiscal-year value, the audit record and the owner segment must all reference the memberId.\n"
  },
