    "result_text": "All 68 tests pass with **BUILD SUCCESS**. The audit output confirms the new format works correctly \u2014 e.g. `NSW267D0C08EF1` = `NSW` (region) + `26` (FY) + `7D0C08EF` (HASH8) + `1` (Luhn CHK).\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit`.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Replaced the `customerCode` schema with `memberId` (documenting the `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` format and dedup suffix), and removed the `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit` schemas. The `OwnerDto` is regenerated from this at build time.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Renamed the persisted field/column `customerCode`/`customer_code` \u2192 `memberId`/`member_id` with matching getter/setter. (It stays persisted because collision handling needs stored state.)\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Removed the `checkDigit` and `membershipNumber` `@Mapping`s and helper methods. `memberId` now maps straight through from the entity by name. `fiscalYear` remains a derived `FY<YY>` field.\n\n4. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 \n   - New `memberId(region, registrationDate, telephone, lastName)` builds `REGION + FY(2-digit) + HASH8 + CHK`, where `HASH8` reuses the same SHA-256-over-(telephone+lastName) first-8-hex and `CHK` is a Luhn digit over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`.\n   - Collision handling (`deduplicateMemberId`) now applies to the `memberId`.\n   - The audit log line and the structured `OWNER_CREATED` event now carry `memberId` instead of `customerCode`/`membershipNumber`.\n\n5. **`db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 Renamed the `customer_code` column to `member_id` (widened to accommodate the longer format plus dedup suffix).\n\nThe relevant checkpoint tests confirm the behavior: `memberId` starts with the region and contains the computed HASH8 (Cp32/Cp56), distinct owners get distinct memberIds (Cp41), the audit event carries the memberId (Cp53), `fiscalYear` stays `FY<YY>` (Cp48), and the old fields are absent (Cp09/14/16/31).",
